Subject: name a Space on hover, above the switcher row

The reference raises the Space's name above the icon row when you hover one,
rather than labelling every icon, which would not fit in a row of them.

The switcher becomes a vertical stack: a name label that is empty most of the
time, and the row of icons beneath it. The label keeps its height whether or not
it has text, so the icons do not jump when a name appears.

A small LabelButton subclass reports enter and exit; views::LabelButton has no
hover callback of its own.

Why: without it a Space is identifiable only by colour, and the tooltip is slow
and does not look like the reference.
Removable when: Spaces are always given icons distinct enough to need no name.
